# QUICKREF — Universal AI Quick Reference Guide

File: openOODA/QUICKREF.oot
Syntax cheat sheet, token economy, and behavioral steering for LLM agents.

## 1. Syntax and Grammar Cheat Sheet

### 1.1 Source Files and Modules
- Code files MUST use extension .oo. Docs MUST use .oot. No .md, .py, .js, .sh.
- Every product .oo file MUST start with a 4-element Academy header:
  // # Module Title
  //
  // Logline: One sentence in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English.
  //
  // Setup: Preconditions and required capabilities.
  //
  // Beats:
  //   1. First action.
  //   2. Second action.
- File length limit: All .oo and .oot files MUST be <= 256 lines.

### 1.2 Functions and Control Flow
- Functions: `pub fn name(arg: Type) -> RetType { ... }` or `fn` for internal.
- Control flow: `if ... else if ... else`, `while cond { ... }`, `for x in xs { ... }`.
- Pattern matching: `match expr { Ok(v) => { ... }, Err(e) => { ... } }`.
- Early return: `return value;`

### 1.3 Structs — No Trailing Commas
  pub type Point = struct {
      x: Int,
      y: Int
  };
  let pt: Point = Point { x: 10, y: 20 };

### 1.4 Mandatory Type Annotation Law
  let count: Int = 0;              // CORRECT
  let mut name: String = "ooda";   // CORRECT
  let val = 42;                    // FORBIDDEN: missing type annotation

---

## 2. Standard Types and Generics

- Int: 64-bit signed integer. Float: 64-bit IEEE-754. Bool: true/false.
- String: Owned UTF-8 string. List[T]: Dynamic ARC array.
- Option[T]: Some(value) or None. Result[T, E]: Ok(value) or Err("reason").

### 2.1 List Operations
  let mut xs: List[Int] = list_new();
  xs = list_push(xs, 10);
  let len: Int = list_len(xs);
  let item: Int = list_get(xs, 0);

### 2.2 Result Handling
  let res: Result[Int, String] = compute();
  match res {
      Ok(v)  => { println("ok: " + v.to_string()); }
      Err(e) => { println("err: " + e); }
  }

---

## 3. Standard Library Modules Map

- std/cli/: CLI parser, ANSI styles, shell completions.
- std/tui/: Double-buffered TUI, flexbox layout, Kitty graphics.
- std/gui/: 3D pipeline, Bezier curves, TrueType parser, GPU canvas.
- std/wui/: WebAssembly UI (VDOM, diff, patch, app).
- std/diag/: Trace spans, telemetry, invariant evaluation.
- std/encoding/: JSON, TOML, CBOR, Base64, CSV parsers.
- std/crypto/: SHA-256, HMAC, Ed25519, ChaCha20, Minisign.
- std/fs/ and std/net/: Sandboxed filesystem and Landlock TCP/UDP.

---

## 4. Capability Security Reference

Pass explicit capability tokens. Never use ambient authority.

| Op             | Required Token      | Fail-closed on |
|----------------|--------------------|-----------------------|
| read_file      | &FsReadCap          | missing token |
| write_file     | &FsWriteCap         | no OODA_FS_WRITEDIR |
| sys_exec       | &ProcessCap         | forged token |
| env_get        | &EnvCap             | non-OODA_ key |
| fetch          | &HttpCap            | missing token |
| tcp_connect    | &TcpCap             | missing token |
| now_ms/sleep   | &TimeCap            | missing token |
| thread_spawn   | &ThreadCap          | missing token |

---

## 5. Token Economy — Sparing Ingress Protocol

Context is finite. Use the product CLI to minimize token consumption.

  # Understand a file (costs ~1.3% of raw source volume)
  ./bin/ooda outline <file.oo>

  # Inspect one symbol (tiny JSON)
  ./bin/ooda reflect <file.oo> [sym]

  # Typecheck only
  ./bin/ooda check <file.oo>

NEVER load these into agent context:
  - ~/.cache/ooda-tmp/**/all*.c     (~700 KB emit dump)
  - Full ROADMAP.oot                (use digest slice)
  - Long gcc error walls            (use ooda err-digest)
  - Full emit-c stdout              (use ooda health)

---

## 6. The 7 Deadly Traps (Zero Tolerance)

Violating any of these causes immediate fail-closed rejection.

  1. No .md, .py, .js, .sh files. Only .oo and .oot.
  2. All files <= 256 lines. No exceptions.
  3. Every .oo file has a 4-element Academy header.
  4. No trailing comma after the last struct field.
  5. No ambient authority. Explicit capability tokens only.
  6. Never copy bin/ooda onto oodac/oodac (fork bomb).
  7. Always double-run tests to prove live execution.

---

## 7. The 5-Step Agent Execution Loop

Execute this loop every turn. Do not skip steps.

  1. OBSERVE   ./bin/ooda outline <target.oo>
  2. CHECK     ./bin/ooda check <target.oo>
  3. ACT       Edit (<=256 lines, Academy header, no trailing commas)
  4. LOCK      ./bin/ooda run <test_smoke.oo>   (run twice)
  5. SHIP      ./bin/ooda run openOODA/scripts/enforcer.oo && commit

---

## 8. Zero-Trust Verification Laws

1. Pure Modules: Keep logic pure. Isolate I/O behind explicit caps.
2. Fail-Closed Returns: Return Result[T, String] with Err on all failures.
3. No Trailing Commas in structs or struct literals.
4. Line Budget: <= 256 lines per file. Split at clean domain seams.
5. Double-Run Mandate: Execute test suites twice to catch non-determinism.
6. Negative Trust: Treat all green passes as suspects until proved live.
